{title: Jamaica Farewell}
{artist: Harry Belafonte}
{key: C}

{c: Verse 1}
[C] Down The Way Where The [F] Nights Are Gay,        And The [G] Sun Shines Daily On The
[C] Mountain Top.        [C] I Took A Trip On A [F] Sailing Ship,
But When I [G] Reached Jamaica I,        [C] Made A Stop.
[C] But Im Sad To Say [Dm] Im On My Way,        [G7] Wont Be Back For [C] Many A Day.
My [C] Heart Is Down, My,        [Dm] Head Is Turning Around;
I Had To [G7] Leave A Little Girl In,        [C] Kingston Town.
[C] But Im Sad To Say [Dm] Im On My Way,        [G7] Wont Be Back For [C] Many A Day.
My [C] Heart Is Down, My,        [Dm] Head Is Turning Around;
I Had To [G7] Leave A Little Girl In,        [C] Kingston Town.
[C] Down At The Market [F] You Can Hear,        Ladies [G] Cry Out While On Their
[C] Heads They Bear,        [C] Akkay Rice, Salt [F] Fish Are Nice,
And The [G] Rum Is Fine Any [C] Time Of Year.        [C] But Im Sad To Say [Dm] Im On My Way,
[G7] Wont Be Back For [C] Many A Day.        My [C] Heart Is Down, My
[Dm] Head Is Turning Around;        I Had To [G7] Leave A Little Girl In
[C] Kingston Town.        [C] Sad To Say [Dm] Im On My Way,
[G7] Wont Be Back For [C] Many A Day.        My [C] Heart Is Down, My
[Dm] Head Is Turning Around;        I Had To [G7] Leave A Little Girl In
[C] Kingston Town.        [C] Sounds Of Laughter [F] Everywhere,
And The [G] Dancing Girls Swirl [C] To And Fro.
[C] I Must Declare [F] My Heart Is There,        Though [G] Ive Been From Maine To [C] Mexico.
[C] But Im Sad To Say [Dm] Im On My Way,        [G7] Wont Be Back For [C] Many A Day.
My [C] Heart Is Down, My,        [Dm] Head Is Turning Around;
I Had To [G7] Leave A Little Girl In,        [C] Kingston Town.
[C] Sad To Say [Dm] Im On My Way,        [G7] Wont Be Back For [C] Many A Day.
My [C] Heart Is Down, My,        [Dm] Head Is Turning Around;
I Had To [G7] Leave A Little Girl In,        [C] Kingston Town.
